# Language

## English

Write these in English:

- Code: identifiers, docstrings, comments, exception messages
- Tests: names, assertion messages
- `.cursor/` rules and skills, `.github/` template headings
- Commit `type` and `scope`, PR titles' type and scope

Chat with the user may be in any language. Issue bodies, PR bodies, and commit subjects may be Japanese.

## Bilingual documents

English is the source of truth. Change both files of a pair in the same PR. Headings stay English.

| English           | Japanese             |
| ----------------- | -------------------- |
| `README.md`       | `README.ja.md`       |
| `docs/roadmap.md` | `docs/roadmap.ja.md` |

Do not add `CONTRIBUTING.md`. The owner's process is `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/`.

Keep the language switch line at the top of both files of a pair. A Japanese-only change must not change the meaning.

## Spec

`docs/design.ja.md` is the spec, in Japanese. Do not add `docs/design.md` until a roadmap row says to translate it. ADRs are English.
